{
  "dom_id": "step-e620",
  "name": "Example: Finding the Acceleration Vector of a Particle Given Its Velocity Vector",
  "problem": "The velocity vector $\\mathbf{v} = \\langle u, v \\rangle$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v} = \\langle 12t+t^2, t^3+1\\rangle.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $\\mathbf{a}$.",
  "worked_solution": "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(12t+{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}+1)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e812+2t,\\,3{t}^{2}\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
